  "summary_en": "Japan's Cabinet-approved AI Basic Plan under the AI Promotion Act (Act No. 53 of 2025). It sets three principles and four policies to make Japan the \"most AI-friendly country\" through deployment, development and governance of \"Trustworthy AI.\" It includes physical AI, AI robots and autonomous driving R&D, plus risk mitigation and annual review.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Established under Article 18(1) of the AI Promotion Act; three principles: innovation with risk mitigation, agile PDCA, integrated domestic-international policy.",
   "Four policies: Adopt AI, Create AI, Enhance AI Trustworthiness (governance), and sustainable transformation toward an AI society.",
   "Promotes R&D and demonstration of physical AI, including public demand for AI robots and advanced autonomous driving.",
   "Develops evaluation platforms and testbeds for AI performance and trustworthiness.",
   "Headquarters monitors implementation with benchmarks; plan revised annually with expert panel input."
